From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:00:00
Subject: [PATCH] Prefer natural antialiasing in DirectWrite regardless of the scale

Without a scale the default hinting preference turns into full hinting,
which renders with GDI_CLASSIC and lays glyphs out with GDI compatible
whole pixel advances and without subpixel positions. A font without
horizontal hints, such as Open Sans 3 hinted in VTT by y only, then lands
at arbitrary subpixel phases inside its rounded cells, so the gaps between
letters vary by a pixel and symmetric letters render lopsided.

Prefer natural antialiasing at any scale, as on scaled screens already:
glyphs keep their natural advances and subpixel positions like in
browsers, while symmetric smoothing is still picked by the effective
pixel size and the gasp table.

diff --git a/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsfontenginedirectwrite.cpp b/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsfontenginedirectwrite.cpp
index ad3efa99591..a7f571aba05 100644
--- a/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsfontenginedirectwrite.cpp
+++ b/src/gui/text/windows/qwindowsfontenginedirectwrite.cpp
@@ -167,12 +167,8 @@ static DWRITE_MEASURING_MODE renderModeToMeasureMode(DWRITE_RENDERING_MODE rende
 static QFont::HintingPreference determineHinting(const QFontDef &fontDef)
 {
     QFont::HintingPreference hintingPreference = QFont::HintingPreference(fontDef.hintingPreference);
-    if (hintingPreference == QFont::PreferDefaultHinting) {
-        if (!qFuzzyCompare(qApp->devicePixelRatio(), 1.0))
-            hintingPreference = QFont::PreferVerticalHinting;
-        else
-            hintingPreference = QFont::PreferFullHinting;
-    }
+    if (hintingPreference == QFont::PreferDefaultHinting)
+        hintingPreference = QFont::PreferVerticalHinting;
 
     return hintingPreference;
 }
